---
import Article from "../layouts/Article.astro";
import { go } from "../data/site";
const toc = [
  { id: "what", label: "What you get" },
  { id: "open", label: "How to open it" },
  { id: "switch", label: "Demo vs real account" },
  { id: "practice", label: "How to practise well" },
];
---

<Article
  title="Pocket Option Demo Account: $50,000 Free, No Registration"
  description="How the Pocket Option demo account works: $50,000 in virtual funds, one-click access without sign-up, top-ups, switching to real money and how to practise properly."
  h1="Pocket Option demo account"
  lead="$50,000 in virtual money, the full platform and no registration. Here is how to get the most out of it before you risk a single dollar."
  crumb="Demo account"
  toc={toc}
>
  <h2 id="what">What you get</h2>
  <p>
    The Pocket Option demo is the real platform running on a virtual balance. Every asset, chart type, indicator and
    trade type is available, so the skills you build carry straight over to a live account.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>$50,000</strong> in virtual funds
    </li>
    <li>No registration needed for the one-click version</li>
    <li>Balance can be topped up again at any time</li>
    <li>Works on web, Android and the iPhone web app</li>
    <li>No time limit</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="open">How to open it</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      Go to Pocket Option and choose <strong>Try demo in one click</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>The platform opens with the demo balance already loaded.</li>
    <li>Optional: create an account so your demo history and settings are saved.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    <a href={go("demo")} rel="sponsored nofollow">
      Open the Pocket Option demo →
    </a>
  </p>

  <h2 id="switch">Demo vs real account</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th></th>
        <th>Demo</th>
        <th>Real</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Balance</td>
        <td>$50,000 virtual</td>
        <td>From $5</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Registration</td>
        <td>Not required</td>
        <td>Email or Google, then verification</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Assets and tools</td>
        <td>All</td>
        <td>All</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Bonuses, tournaments</td>
        <td>No</td>
        <td>Yes</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Withdrawals</td>
        <td>No</td>
        <td>Yes</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    Switching is done from the balance menu in the top right corner. Your demo stays available after you deposit, so you
    can keep testing ideas without touching real funds.
  </p>

  <h2 id="practice">How to practise well</h2>
  <p>
    A $50,000 balance makes it tempting to place large trades. That habit is expensive on a real account. Treat the demo
    as if it held the amount you actually plan to deposit.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Set a demo budget equal to your planned first deposit, for example $50.</li>
    <li>Risk no more than 1 to 2% of that budget per trade.</li>
    <li>Pick two or three assets and learn how they move at different times of day.</li>
    <li>Keep a simple journal: asset, direction, timeframe, reason, result.</li>
    <li>Move to real money only after a few weeks of consistent results.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Our <a href="/how-to-trade/">trading walkthrough</a> explains the platform screen by screen.
  </p>
</Article>
